During the 1999 tech bubble, Cisco CSCO) traded at 200x earnings, far exceeding Grahamʼs
recommended P/E of 1520x. Defensive investors avoided such speculative stocks, while
enterprising investors shorted overvalued equities. By 2002, CSCO fell 80%, validating
Grahamʼs warnings .
